<article class="env-corollary" id="02XN">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02XN">Corollary <span data-tag="02XN">7.1.8.14</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories, let $B$ be a simplicial set, and let $F^{B}: \operatorname{Fun}(B,\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}(B, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ be given by composition with $F$. If $\overline{f}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}(B,\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ is a levelwise $F$-colimit diagram (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="06A7" href="/tag/06A7">7.1.8.13</a>), then it is an $F^{B}$-colimit diagram. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Proposition <a data-tag="02XK" href="/tag/02XK">7.1.8.10</a> in the special case $A = \emptyset $. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
